__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.git/
.github/
*.pyc
*.pyo
tests/
# Package-owned tests (features/*/tests/, adapters/*/tests/, ...).
# A bare `tests/` is anchored to the context root, so it excluded the
# root suite ONLY -- once the test files moved next to the code they
# guard, all 274 of them (3.0M) started shipping in the image.  Verified
# with a build probe, not read off the docs.
**/tests/
conftest.py
pytest.ini
# Package documentation (capabilities/*/docs/, features/*/docs/, ...).
# Same anchoring trap as tests/: the root `docs/` line above this
# block's sibling only excludes the ROOT docs tree, so the moment laws
# and runbooks moved next to the code they document, they would start
# shipping in the image.
**/docs/
backups/
*.log
.bot.pid
.pid
.env
.venv/
venv/
env/
*.tar.gz
interfaces/dashboard/node_modules/
interfaces/dashboard/dist/
interfaces/miniapp/node_modules/
interfaces/miniapp/dist/
interfaces/system_dashboard/node_modules/
interfaces/system_dashboard/dist/
data/
scripts/
mypy.ini
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
# Secrets that must NEVER land in an image layer — the Dockerfile's
# `COPY . .` would otherwise bake them in.  Google service-account keys
# have been named both semi-telematics-*.json and truck-*.json; a bare
# *.json is too broad (locale/config files), so match the key shapes.
semi-telematics-*.json
truck-*.json
*-service-account*.json

# Docs, Claude Code config, editor state — never belong in the image
# build context (the app serves nothing from them; docs/ alone is MBs).
docs/
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
